  "definitions": {
   "overhang": "faces with n.b < -cos(angle) (strict), n the outward face normal and b the unit build direction (up); the angle is measured from the plate; plate-contact faces are not counted; a face within about 1e-15 of the limit can fall on either side (floating point)",
   "plate_contact": "faces with n.b < -0.99 whose centre is less than 0.3 mm above the lowest point along b",
   "support_volume": "estimate of the space under the overhang faces: sum over the faces of (free gap down to the plate or to the part) x (projected face area), in mm3; a solid-column upper bound, real supports use less material; for up to 30000 faces (random sample, fixed seed) scaled to the full overhang area",
   "bed_fit": "extents_mm are the part extents in the build frame (two in-plane extents and the height). The footprint is the part projected on the plate. For a turn about the build axis of 0 to 89 degrees in 1-degree steps, the margin is the smaller of the two spare lengths: bed side minus footprint side, the sides sorted (so a turn of 90 degrees is the same as 0). For a part in the middle of the bed, the gap to each edge is half of the spare length. bed_turn_deg is the turn with the largest margin. If the part fits as it is, a turn is reported only if it gains at least 10 mm of margin; otherwise bed_turn_deg is 0. bed_footprint_mm is the footprint at that turn and bed_margin_mm that margin. bed_fit is true if the margin is not negative. If no turn fits, bed_margin_mm is negative: the footprint is that many mm longer than the bed at the best turn. The height is not limited",
   "thinnest_member": "estimate: percentile 1 of the inward chord lengths (surface point along the negative face normal to the first wall), in mm. It means: 1 percent of the sampled surface area has a thinner chord. A thin feature on less than about 1 percent of the area does not move it: see area_below_mm2. min_mm is the shortest chord of the sample; it includes noise from sharp edges. A value equal to max_chord_mm means that many mm or more",
   "area_below_mm2": "surface area (mm2) whose chord is thinner than each threshold in mm: the share of the sampled chords below the threshold times the total area; area_below_pct is the same share in percent. The sampling error of a share f is about sqrt(f (1 - f) / samples)"
  },
